<main class="stub wrap" id="main">

  <div class="panel">
    <h2>Before the course — optional refreshers</h2>
    <p class="lead">Not required prework. Useful if you haven't completed Responsible AI Leadership, or want the core ideas fresh.</p>
    <div class="refgrid">
      <a class="ref" href="https://www.aim.com.au/blog/wrap-up-responsible-ai-leadership" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
        <div class="rt">Responsible AI Leadership — Webinar Insights</div>
        <div class="rm">AIM · blog wrap-up</div>
        <p>The webinar and write-up covering the responsible AI leadership foundations this course builds on.</p>
        <span class="go">Open →</span>
      </a>
      <a class="ref" href="https://www.aim.com.au/digital-skills/courses/responsible-ai-leadership" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
        <div class="rt">Responsible AI Leadership — the course</div>
        <div class="rm">AIM · 2-day short course</div>
        <p>The prerequisite course: AI leadership stance, defensible decisions, evaluating outputs, guardrails, incidents and change.</p>
        <span class="go">Open →</span>
      </a>
    </div>
    <div class="refband" style="margin-top:14px">
      <h4>Already have the Responsible AI Leadership workbook?</h4>
      <p style="margin-bottom:6px">Your five carried-in foundations link straight to its modules from the <a href="welcome.html" style="color:var(--coral-dark);font-weight:600">Welcome page</a> — or open <a href="../../responsible-ai-leadership/index.html" style="color:var(--teal-dark);font-weight:600">the RAIL interactive workbook</a> directly (its own access code applies).</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="panel">
    <h2>Australian frameworks &amp; obligations</h2>
    <div class="refgrid">
      <a class="ref" href="https://www.legislation.gov.au/C2024A00128/asmade/text" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
        <div class="rt">Privacy and Other Legislation Amendment Act 2024</div>
        <div class="rm">Australian Government · 2024</div>
        <p>Mandatory transparency obligations for automated decision-making (effective 10 Dec 2026), a statutory tort for serious invasions of privacy, and strengthened enforcement powers.</p>
        <span class="go">Read the Act →</span>
      </a>
      <a class="ref" href="https://www.industry.gov.au/publications/australias-ai-ethics-principles" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
        <div class="rt">Australia's AI Ethics Principles</div>
        <div class="rm">Dept of Industry, Science and Resources · 2019</div>
        <p>Eight voluntary principles for responsible AI design, development and deployment in the Australian context.</p>
        <span class="go">Open →</span>
      </a>
      <a class="ref" href="https://www.digital.gov.au/ai/ai-in-government-policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
        <div class="rt">Policy for the Responsible Use of AI in Government, v2.0</div>
        <div class="rm">Digital Transformation Agency · 2025</div>
        <p>Mandatory requirements for AI governance in the Australian public sector.</p>
        <span class="go">Open →</span>
      </a>
      <a class="ref" href="https://www.finance.gov.au/sites/default/files/2020-12/Information-Sheet-Overview-Risk-Management-Process.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
        <div class="rt">An Overview of the Risk Management Process</div>
        <div class="rm">Dept of Finance · 2020 · based on AS/NZS ISO 31000</div>
        <p>A free, publicly accessible overview of a risk-criteria framework — useful behind the Four Autonomy Decision Lenses.</p>
        <span class="go">Open the PDF →</span>
      </a>
      <a class="ref" href="https://www.apra.gov.au/information-security" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
        <div class="rt">CPG 234 Information Security</div>
        <div class="rm">APRA · Prudential Practice Guide · 2019</div>
        <p>Incident response, notification obligations and control frameworks for APRA-regulated entities — banks, insurers and super funds.</p>
        <span class="go">Open →</span>
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="panel">
    <h2>Standards &amp; governance frameworks</h2>
    <div class="refgrid">
      <a class="ref" href="https://www.iso.org/home/insights-news/resources/iso-42001-explained-what-it-is.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
        <div class="rt">ISO/IEC 42001:2023 — AI Management Systems</div>
        <div class="rm">ISO · 2023</div>
        <p>The first international standard specifically for AI management systems: lifecycle governance, risk assessment, controls and continuous improvement.</p>
        <span class="go">ISO 42001 explained →</span>
      </a>
      <a class="ref" href="https://www.nist.gov/publications/artificial-intelligence-risk-management-framework-ai-rmf-10" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
        <div class="rt">AI Risk Management Framework (AI RMF 1.0)</div>
        <div class="rm">NIST · 2023</div>
        <p>The foundational voluntary framework for governing AI risk — Govern, Map, Measure and Manage.</p>
        <span class="go">Open →</span>
      </a>
      <a class="ref" href="https://oecd.ai/en/ai-principles" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
        <div class="rt">OECD AI Principles</div>
        <div class="rm">OECD · 2024</div>
        <p>Transparency, explainability and accountability as core requirements for trustworthy AI — referenced by Australian and international frameworks.</p>
        <span class="go">Open →</span>
      </a>
      <a class="ref" href="https://govtech-responsibleai.github.io/agentic-risk-capability-framework/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
        <div class="rt">The Agentic Risk &amp; Capability Framework</div>
        <div class="rm">Khoo, Foo &amp; Lee · 2025 · arXiv:2512.22211</div>
        <p>“With Great Capabilities Come Great Responsibilities” — a technical governance framework for risks specific to agentic AI systems.</p>
        <span class="go">Open →</span>
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="panel">
    <h2>Evidence &amp; industry reading</h2>
    <div class="refgrid">
      <a class="ref" href="https://www.canlii.org/en/bc/bccrt/doc/2024/2024bccrt149/2024bccrt149.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
        <div class="rt">Moffatt v Air Canada, 2024 BCCRT 149</div>
        <div class="rm">BC Civil Resolution Tribunal · 14 Feb 2024</div>
        <p>The ruling that established organisational liability for AI chatbot misrepresentation — accountability did not transfer to the technology.</p>
        <span class="go">Read the ruling →</span>
      </a>
      <a class="ref" href="https://www.deloitte.com/us/en/what-we-do/capabilities/applied-artificial-intelligence/content/state-of-ai-in-the-enterprise.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
        <div class="rt">State of AI in the Enterprise 2026</div>
        <div class="rm">Deloitte Insights · 2025</div>
        <p>3,235 senior leaders across 24 countries on AI adoption, agentic AI readiness and governance maturity.</p>
        <span class="go">Open →</span>
      </a>
      <a class="ref" href="https://www.deloitte.com/us/en/insights/topics/technology-management/tech-trends/2026/agentic-ai-strategy.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
        <div class="rt">Agentic AI Strategy — Tech Trends 2026, Ch. 2</div>
        <div class="rm">Deloitte Insights · 2026</div>
        <p>Infrastructure, workflow redesign and the strategic shift from AI pilots to production-ready agentic systems.</p>
        <span class="go">Open →</span>
      </a>
      <a class="ref" href="https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/worklab/work-trend-index/2025-the-year-thefrontier-firm-is-born" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
        <div class="rt">2025: The Year the Frontier Firm Is Born</div>
        <div class="rm">Microsoft WorkLab · Work Trend Index · 2025</div>
        <p>Microsoft's research on human-agent teams and the emergence of AI-operated workflows.</p>
        <span class="go">Open →</span>
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="panel">
    <h2>Where next</h2>
    <div class="refband">
      <h4>Designing Workflows for Agentic AI</h4>
      <p style="margin-bottom:6px">This course decided <i>whether and under what conditions</i> agents may act. AIM's companion course goes a level deeper — designing, delegating and supervising the workflows themselves. <a href="https://www.aim.com.au/digital-skills/courses/designing-workflows-for-agentic-ai" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="go">Course details →</a> <span class="small">·</span> <a href="../../agentic-ai/index.html" class="go">Its interactive workbook →</a> <span class="small">(own access code)</span></p>
    </div>
  </div>

